{"id": "unknown-2026-10-09-013", "date": "2026-10-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["green_hydrogen_cost"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "The Hydrogen Stream: Dutch researchers calculate green H2 costs as low as €7.2/kg", "content": "<p>Researchers at the University of Groningen have calculated green hydrogen production costs of €7.2/kg to €7.3/kg using renewable power purchase agreements and hybrid electricity supply configurations, compared with €7.7/kg for wholesale electricity sourcing. The study found that long-term revenue guarantees are essential to making large-scale hydrogen projects financially viable.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/09/the-hydrogen-stream-dutch-researchers-calculate-gr", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/09/the-hydrogen-stream-dutch-researchers-calculate-green-h2-costs-as-low-as-e7-2-kg/", "type": "rss"}]}
